1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,500
Danny had built something
real on that street.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,500
Six years.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,000
You could smell the fryer
before you reached the door.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The regulars knew the specials
before the board went up.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
But then a Monday came
quiet. No reason.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Just... quiet.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
And Danny did what most of
us do — he went looking.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Every Sunday after that —
the one morning he'd kept for himself —

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
he spent reading other
people's Google pages.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Counting stars he couldn't
close the gap on.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
No. Not today.

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
That thing has taken
enough Sundays.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,500
He told me later —
it wasn't a decision.

14
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:40,000
It was just a dog, a table, and a man
remembering what a Sunday was for.

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Some things can't
be gamed back.

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
But some things
can be kept.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,500
I'm Bella — ciao for now.
